      "body": "Found it \u2014 cell `4ed04321` fails with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'torch'` because this notebook's kernel is misconfigured. Notebook `0_dataset_dataloader_template.ipynb` uses kernelspec `conda-env-jovyan-surya_ws-py` (the `/home/jovyan/envs/surya_ws` env, which has torch 2.9.1), but `1_baseline_template.ipynb` uses kernelspec `python3` (the base `notebook` conda env, which has no torch). Both kernels are registered via `nb_conda_kernels`, so the fix is just pointing notebook 1 at the same kernel as notebook 0.",
