      "body": "The error: `ValueError: mask_dir must be provided for FlareDSDataset` in cell `70e9c5b2` (the `build_helio_dataloaders` call). Two things are wrong, both the same copy-paste-from-template mistake we already fixed elsewhere in this app:\n\n1. Cell `34db2cc6` imports `FlareDSDataset` from `downstream_apps.template.datasets.template_dataset` \u2014 the generic template's dataset (a simple flux-regression class with no mask support). It should import from `downstream_apps.sf_triggers.datasets.sf_triggers_dataset`, the app's actual dataset (which needs `mask_dir`/`mask_time_tolerance`), exactly like notebook 0 already does.\n2. Cell `70e9c5b2`'s call to `build_helio_dataloaders(...)` never passes `mask_dir`/`mask_time_tolerance` through, so once the import is corrected, `FlareDSDataset.__init__` still raises on the missing `mask_dir`.\n\nLet me fix both.",
